LICENCE NOTES FOR BUNDLED DATA
==============================

The termpremia package is released under the MIT licence (see LICENSE).

Datasets distributed with the package are NOT all covered by that licence.
Each is governed by the terms of its own source, recorded below. Where those
terms are more restrictive than MIT, they govern.


1. acm_published  --  Federal Reserve Bank of New York
--------------------------------------------------------------------

Source: Treasury Term Premia
        https://www.newyorkfed.org/research/data_indicators/term-premia-tabs
        https://www.newyorkfed.org/medialibrary/media/research/data_indicators/ACMTermPremium.xls

Redistributed under the New York Fed's Terms of Use
(https://www.newyorkfed.org/privacy/termsofuse), which permit downloading,
storing, copying and distributing their content subject to three conditions.
All three are met as follows.

  (a) Attribution. Source identifiers and copyright notices are retained:

        (c) Federal Reserve Bank of New York. Content from the New York Fed
        subject to the Terms of Use at newyorkfed.org.

  (b) Modifications clearly labelled. The following changes were made to the
      published workbook. No values were altered.

        - Only the "ACM Monthly" sheet is retained; the daily sheet is dropped.
        - The series are reshaped from wide (one column per tenor) to long.
        - The sample is truncated at 2024-12-31 so the snapshot is stable.

      The reshaping is performed by data-raw/acm.R, which is included in the
      source repository so the transformation is fully reproducible.

  (c) Same permissions passed on. Anyone receiving this package receives
      acm_published under these same terms, conditions and restrictions --
      not under the MIT licence. Redistributing it onward requires carrying
      this notice with it.


2. gsw_monthly  --  Federal Reserve Board
--------------------------------------------------------------------

Source: Series feds200628, "Nominal Yield Curve"
        https://www.federalreserve.gov/data/nominal-yield-curve.htm

A Federal Reserve Board staff research product. No copyright is asserted on
the source page and no terms of use restrict redistribution. It is not an
official statistical release and is subject to revision without notice.

Derived from the published Svensson parameters rather than copied verbatim:
the curve is re-evaluated on a monthly maturity grid by data-raw/gsw.R.
Please cite the underlying research:

  Gurkaynak, R. S., B. Sack and J. H. Wright (2007). "The U.S. Treasury yield
  curve: 1961 to the present." Journal of Monetary Economics 54(8), 2291-2304.


Notes on data not bundled
--------------------------------------------------------------------

Philadelphia Fed Survey of Professional Forecasters (BILL10, TBILL) is NOT
distributed with this package. The Philadelphia Fed asserts copyright with all
rights reserved and limits use to informational, educational and research
purposes. That is a use restriction rather than a redistribution grant, and it
is incompatible with an MIT-licensed package usable for any purpose. Survey
functionality therefore relies on a download helper plus a clearly-labelled
synthetic fixture for tests.
